-- `Never` is written `⊥` (language.md §12.10): `never_spelling_removed`
-- at a `Never` that names `Basics`' empty type, through the prelude (8:5)
-- and qualified (12:5), and the type is the same — `never` takes it — so
-- nothing else is reported. A module's own `Never` is another type.
import Other


a : Never → Int
a v = never v


b : Basics.Never → Int
b v = never v


c : Other.Never → Other.Never
c v = v
